/*
Expected output:
check
always 1
always 2
after 2

A check block with an always block and no detect block. Nothing goes wrong
in the check block, so the always block runs once, then the program carries
on. The second check block is empty, which the compiler handles on its own
path, and its always block must still run.

The variable count is declared before the check, so it shares the action's
local variable slots with anything the compiler stores while running the
always block. Its value must come through unchanged.
*/

class Main
    action Main
        integer count = 0
        check
            output "check"
        always
            count = count + 1
            output "always " + count
        end

        check
        always
            count = count + 1
            output "always " + count
        end
        output "after " + count
    end
end
